{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Remember Avraham, etc.</b> The intention is not regarding the oath, for HaShem had already answered him that He would fulfill His oath through the seed of Moshe and they would become a great nation, and that is the seed of the patriarchs as well. Rather, it comes to say that the men would be greatly distressed by the occurrence. It also comes with the argument that He needs to remember their merit, for the reason that He stated in the Ten Commandments (Exodus 20:6): ״וְעֹשֶׂה חֶסֶד לַאֲלָפִים לְאֹהֲבַי״ — and that is His saying <b>Your servants</b>, and His saying <b>to whom You swore</b>, etc.; all this is to magnify the attainment of the patriarchs from the aspect of love." "<b>And all this land, etc.</b> The interpretations here are many, and there are those who explain that these are the words of Moshe, who said before HaShem what I have said to them, etc. And it is possible to say that these are the words of HaShem, and the meaning of <b>I said</b> is an expression of elevation, on the pattern of (Isaiah 3:10) ״אִמְרוּ צַדִּיק״. And this is the meaning of <b>all the land</b>, etc., which I have exalted above all other lands, <b>I will give</b>, etc. And so we find that the verse states (Deuteronomy 11:12) ״אֶרֶץ אֲשֶׁר וְגוֹ׳ עֵינֵי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ״, etc., and the intention in this is to recall their merit before Him."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:35:59.090089157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}